  "prefLabel": "Env-Hw 1402.03 Mixtures of Used Oil and Characteristic Hazardous Waste",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Env-Hw 1402.03 Mixtures of Used Oil and Characteristic Hazardous Waste.\n\n(a) Except as provided in (b), below, a mixture of used oil and any characteristic hazardous waste shall be regulated as a hazardous waste, rather than used oil under this chapter.\n\n(b) A mixture of used oil and ignitable-only hazardous waste shall be managed under this chapter if:\n\n(1) A representative sample of the hazardous waste prior to mixing is hazardous only for the characteristic of ignitability as specified in Env-Hw 403.03(b);\n\n(2) A representative sample of the used oil and hazardous waste mixture has a flash point greater than 140°F; and\n\n(3) The used oil handler creating the mixture maintains documentation onsite documenting satisfaction of the requirements of (b)(1) and (2), above, for 3 years from the date the mixture was last handled.\n\nSource. #14282, eff 8-1-25, EXPIRES: 8-1-35",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/env-hw1400.html"
